# Intent: keep scripts and game-relevant text readable; hide generated junk,
# binaries, and bulky Unity YAML assets. Filenames remain visible via Glob.

# === Unity Generated & Heavy Folders ===
Library/
Temp/
obj/
Build/
Builds/
Logs/
UserSettings/
ProjectSettings/
Packages/
!Packages/manifest.json   # exception: package version source of truth

# === Bulky Unity YAML Assets (text, but huge — filename-only is enough) ===
*.prefab
*.unity
*.mat
*.anim
*.controller
*.mixer

# === Binary Asset Files ===
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tga
*.psd
*.tif
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg
*.fbx
*.obj
*.blend
*.dll
*.pdb

# === ScriptableObject .asset files — INTENTIONALLY NOT IGNORED ===
# They are text YAML. CLAUDE.md rule applies: "may be read when directly
# required — ask first." Keeping them out of this file aligns the two rule
# sources so the exception is actually honourable.

# === Meta files — INTENTIONALLY NOT IGNORED ===
# Small text YAML containing script GUIDs and import settings. The dashboard
# pulls ITEM_SCRIPT_GUID / SPELL_SCRIPT_GUID from these. Keep readable.

# === Visual Studio / Rider / IDE files ===
.vs/
.idea/
*.csproj
*.sln
*.user
*.userprefs

# === Claude-specific (memory/settings hidden, but rules/ stay readable) ===
.claudeignore
CLAUDE.md
.claude/settings*
.claude/projects/

# === Other junk ===
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
